The MIT terms above cover the software: everything under src/, tests/, docs/
and the sample tracks under sample-data/.

They do NOT cover one bundled data file. src/rcta/data/airports.json is a
database derived in part from OpenFlights, which is published under the Open
Database License, and share-alike follows the data rather than the code. That
file is therefore licensed under ODbL 1.0; see src/rcta/data/LICENSE for the
terms and the attributions that go with it.

Nothing else in src/rcta/data/ is affected: airlines.json, providers.json and
flight_providers.json are this project's own work and are MIT like the rest.
